## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, native Apple (SwiftUI) port of the **CronParser** devtools surface at parity with `web/src/features/admin/components/devtools/tools/CronParser.tsx`, following the established sibling pattern (ByteSizeConverter 0012, TimestampTool 0021).

**Delivered (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/CronParser.*`, 7 files, 1506 lines):**
- **Adapter** — pure ports of `describeCron`, `getNextCronRuns` (with the exact `matchField` `* / , -` precedence quirks), `formatDateTime`, field-splitting, and presets.
- **Model** — `@Observable` state holder (P1/S8), i18n facade (P1/S10), `view.opened` telemetry seam (P1/S11).
- **View + Views** — ToolCard header (green `timer` icon), expression `Input`, wrapping ghost preset buttons, the green Description panel, and the Next-Runs list (info-tone numbered chip + mono dates). Every state renders (empty / content-with-runs / content-no-runs) — never a blank box.
- **Previews, Tests, strings catalog.**

**Verification — surface GREEN:**
- swiftformat `--lint` 0/6 · swiftlint `--strict` 0 violations · placeholder gate `PLACEHOLDER_COUNT=0` (+ self-test proves the scanner)
- Foundation adapter harness **21/21** web-parity oracles · isolated SwiftPM XCTest **30/30** under Swift 6
- Real **iOS-18 + macOS-15 `swiftc -typecheck` = 0 errors** against the real `Tokens.swift` + real shared components
- `xcodegen generate` enumerates all 7 files · collision-free · all 10 web i18n keys present · a11y labels on every interactive element

**Full-app `xcodebuild build test` — BLOCKED (pre-existing, unrelated, captured first-hand):**
- iOS: KMP `Shared.xcframework` built+staged and the whole module type-checked, then a **Swift 6.3.2 `swift-frontend` IRGen crash** (`report_at_maximum_capacity`) on an **unrelated** batch (AnomalyInlineRow/AppCommands/AppearanceSettings). **Zero CronParser diagnostics** anywhere.
- macOS: **dev-signing** (`0 valid identities`).

These are exactly the blocks `apps/macos-pending-verifications.md` defers to the macOS acceptance gate. Evidence is in `.github/prompts/monorepo/logs/p4-apple-feature-views-0014-CronParser.log`, ending `EXIT=65` / `STATUS=BLOCKED` with platform-capability evidence (the sanctioned terminal state).

